  "articleBody": "Hiring the right finish carpenter makes the difference between kitchen cabinets that sit level and trim that pulls apart over time. Before you approve an estimate or sign an agreement for finish carpentry, here is what to confirm to ensure your project goes smoothly.\n\nQuestions to Ask Before You Decide\n- What exact millwork is included in your scope? Confirm whether the quote covers cabinet fillers, toe kicks, crown molding, light rails, end panels, hardware installation, door adjustments, and final caulk or touch-ups.\n- Does the work include custom fitting on-site? Prebuilt cabinets frequently require scribing and trimming to fit out-of-plumb walls and uneven subfloors.\n- Who supplies the fasteners, trim, and matching fillers? Clarify whether you supply these materials or if the carpenter sources them.\n- How do you protect finished drywall and flooring? Carpentry generates dust and involves heavy components, so surface protection should be clear.\n\nWhen to Call a Professional\nUneven subfloors, bowed drywall, and complex crown molding profiles call for experienced hands. Because countertop installers template directly off base cabinets, even slight leveling errors can create expensive headaches.\n\nIf you are planning kitchen finish carpentry in the Denver metro area, reach out to Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to discuss your layout and get an honest, detailed quote.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
